.TH MAR 1 "October 2026" "mar 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mar \- Universal Data Container and high-performance archival utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mar
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mar
is a high-performance archive utility and Universal Data Container format designed for efficient storage,
random access, network streaming, and retrieval of large datasets. It features block-based multi-threaded
compression, content deduplication, fast indexing, and algebraic subset slicing.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose progress output. Can be specified multiple times for increased detail.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error output.
.TP
.BR \-\-stopwatch
Report overall command execution time.
.TP
.BR \-\-version
Display the tool version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B create \fIarchive\fR [\fIfiles...\fR]
Create a new MAR archive from files or directories.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compression " \fIalgo\fR"
Compression algorithm: \fBzstd\fR (default), \fBlz4\fR, \fBgzip\fR, \fBbzip2\fR, or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-compression\-level " \fIn\fR"
Compression level (-1 for codec default).
.TP
.BR \-\-checksum " \fItype\fR"
Integrity checksum algorithm: \fBxxhash3\fR (default), \fBblake3\fR, \fBcrc32c\fR, or \fBnone\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-block\-size " \fIsize\fR"
Target block size (e.g., 64KB, 1MB, 4MB; default 1MB).
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " \fInum\fR"
Number of worker threads (default: hardware concurrency).
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Overwrite existing output archive.
.TP
.BR \-\-dedup
Deduplicate identical files by content hash (requires \fB--hashes\fR).
.RE
.TP
.B import \fB-o\fR \fIoutput.mar\fR \fIarchive.tar\fR...
Import one or more TAR archives directly into a MAR archive without extracting them to disk.
.TP
.B slice \fIarchive\fR \fB-o\fR \fIdest.mar\fR [\fIpatterns...\fR]
Extract a subset of files into a new MAR archive using algebraic inclusion/exclusion patterns.
.RS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-include " \fIpattern\fR"
Include files matching glob pattern.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude " \fIpattern\fR"
Exclude files matching glob pattern.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-files\-from " \fIfile\fR"
Read list of files or include patterns from file (- for standard input).
.RE
.TP
.B extract \fIarchive\fR [\fB-o\fR \fIdir\fR] [\fIfiles...\fR]
Extract files from an archive to a destination directory.
.TP
.B list \fIarchive\fR
List the names of all files contained in the archive.
.TP
.B get \fIarchive\fR \fIfilename\fR
Extract a specific file to standard output or a destination directory.
.TP
.B cat \fIarchive\fR [\fIfiles...\fR]
Dump file contents to standard output or as structured JSON.
.TP
.B diff \fIarchive1\fR \fIarchive2\fR
Compare two archives and output file differences.
.TP
.B delta \fB-o\fR \fIdelta.mar\fR \fIbase.mar\fR \fInew.mar\fR
Create a binary delta archive representing modifications between two versions.
.TP
.B redact \fIarchive\fR \fIfiles...\fR
Zero-out file contents while preserving archive layout and file records.
.TP
.B index \fIarchive\fR
Create a fast sidecar search index for an archive.
.TP
.B search \fIarchive\fR \fIquery\fR
Search archive entries using the sidecar index.
.TP
.B hash \fIarchive\fR
Compute a deterministic archive hash (\fBxxhash64\fR or \fBblake3\fR).
.TP
.B header \fIarchive\fR
Display archive header structure, block counts, and metadata.
.TP
.B validate \fIarchive\fR
Validate archive block checksums and data integrity.
.TP
.B version
Display tool version and specification format version.
